575fb145987a7","event_uuid":"a5de0d64-4a1c-4415-bfaa-ef360f7ec179","position":{"commit_sha":"1b30bd04441d2edc198dce0e0cb854c93fb3506b","position":"1786651962938148001-a5de0d64-4a1c-4415-bfaa-ef360f7ec179"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"351623ae24cb6fd2c19e3304236c9e77c45d72eac8d9c3b1a5df1aca752957f9","event_uuid":"bc3c2575-730b-431f-ae80-9c2bab3e3e9b","position":{"commit_sha":"a69737ae9cf885e90d4fbb2e3f90219e1cd7e8a7","position":"1786652293953810001-bc3c2575-730b-431f-ae80-9c2bab3e3e9b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"504f21de144ec6aa4783905fbff5d6b4d539a589555e0ac30c8d8031aa8ddd22","event_uuid":"39606cc0-2952-46c9-95fc-0196d0eeaeff","position":{"commit_sha":"a69737ae9cf885e90d4fbb2e3f90219e1cd7e8a7","position":"1786652295298409001-39606cc0-2952-46c9-95fc-0196d0eeaeff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d01018f141afdb6fd4cbe076800bd1d848d628d54007415e97023c7dfc548273","event_uuid":"493a3e75-995c-4826-909f-8efbddaa9c9c","position":{"commit_sha":"b7a1d619002a9e3d9683351bdf63717cb97b9201","position":"1786654754206722575-493a3e75-995c-4826-909f-8efbddaa9c9c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786162204055891001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"493a3e75-995c-4826-909f-8efbddaa9c9c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6d88-0c78-637b-4d4b"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py` measures **771 lines** against the hard 800-line\nmodule-size gate (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), which CI enforces with no allowlist. The sibling\nstory that fans the fetch out over several projects rewrites the query construction in\n`_build_snapshot` and will not fit in 29 lines.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract the pagination cluster into a new `fetch_paging.py`: `_ACLI_CEILING` and\n`SilentTruncationError` (`:99-120`), `_extract_issues` (`:251-262`), `_iter_pages` (`:265-390`) and\n`collect` (`:392-399`).\n\nThe call chain is genuine and self-contained: `collect` calls `_iter_pages` (`:397`), which calls\n`_extract_issues` (`:296`) and raises `SilentTruncationError` (`:308,343,355`) against\n`_ACLI_CEILING` (`:354`). Nothing in the cluster calls back upward; `_build_snapshot` reaches it only\nthrough `_iter_pages` (`:554`). The new module's complete import list is `annotations` and a\n`TYPE_CHECKING` import of `TicketTransport` — the pagination code is otherwise pure.\n\nThis extraction is well matched to the incoming change, which rewrites the `queries` tuple at\n`_build_snapshot:548-554` into a per-project loop over `jqls_for` — all of which stays in `fetcher.py`.\n\n**Three things must stay resident**, and getting any of them wrong breaks tests silently:\n\n- `_DONE_RECENT_CAP` (`:105`) stays — `_build_snapshot:550` uses it. Only `_ACLI_CEILING` moves.\n- `_load_acli` and `_load_alert_store` stay — they carry **25** and **3** `patch.object(fetcher, ...)`\n  sites respectively, and a module-attribute patch does not survive a module move. Both are called\n  from `_build_snapshot` (`:523,536`), which stays, so no patch site is disturbed.\n- `fetcher.py` re-exports **all four** moved names — `_iter_pages`, `collect`,\n  `SilentTruncationError` and `_ACLI_CEILING` — because every one of them is reached as an attribute\n  of `fetcher` by existing tests, and an attribute access does not follow a moved symbol:\n  - `hasattr(fetcher, \"_iter_pages\")` and `hasattr(fetcher, \"collect\")`\n    (`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_snapshot.py:118,139`), plus further\n    `fetcher._iter_pages` / `fetcher.collect` accesses in the same file and in\n    `test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py`;\n  - `fetcher.SilentTruncationError`\n    (`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_pagination_jql.py:133,165`) as well as the\n    explicit `from rebar_reconciler.fetcher import SilentTruncationError` at\n    `test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py:32`;\n  - `fetcher._ACLI_CEILING` (`test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py:149`), which reads the constant\n    directly to size its fixture. This one is easy to miss precisely because the constant looks\n    private and unshared.\n\nThe re-export keeps roughly 48 existing references green across six test modules. Note that the two\nproduction mentions of `fetcher._iter_pages` — `_backend.py:62` and\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py:139,153` — are **docstring prose** recording bug history, not\nruntime references, so no production module needs an edit.\n\nThis is a behaviour-preserving move: no logic is rewritten.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetch_paging.py` (new) — the moved cluster, ~195 lines\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py` — drops to ~606 lines, plus a re-export block\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new behaviour, so the oracle is the existing suite passing unchanged. The risks are attribute\npresence and patch survival, so both are asserted rather than assumed:\n\n- Attribute-surface assertion: `hasattr(fetcher, \"_iter_pages\")` and `hasattr(fetcher, \"collect\")`\n  both hold after the move, and `SilentTruncationError` still imports from `fetcher`.\n- Patch survival: the tests that `patch.object(fetcher, \"_load_acli\")` and `\"_load_alert_store\"` pass\n  unedited, proving those symbols stayed resident and are still resolved from `fetcher`'s globals.\n- Truncation behaviour preserved: a fixture exceeding `_ACLI_CEILING` still raises\n  `SilentTruncationError` through the real `collect → _iter_pages` path — the contract most at risk\n  from moving the constant away from its raiser.\n- One-way import: `fetch_paging` must not import `fetcher`, asserted directly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `fetcher.py` and `fetch_paging.py` are each at or below 650 lines; checked by the module-size\n      gate with both counts recorded.\n- [ ] All four moved names — `_iter_pages`, `collect`, `SilentTruncationError` and `_ACLI_CEILING` —\n      still resolve as attributes of `fetcher`; checked by a test asserting each by attribute access,\n      which covers the two existing `hasattr` assertions and the direct `fetcher._ACLI_CEILING` read.\n- [ ] `_load_acli`, `_load_alert_store` and `_DONE_RECENT_CAP` remain defined in `fetcher.py`;\n      checked by asserting each is in that module's own namespace, not merely importable.\n- [ ] A fixture exceeding the ceiling still raises `SilentTruncationError` via the real paging path;\n      checked by the existing pagination held-out test running unedited.\n- [ ] `fetch_paging.py` does not import `fetcher`; checked by a test importing the two modules in\n      both orders and asserting `fetcher` is absent from `fetch_paging`'s imports.\n- [ ] The full existing test suite passes with no test-file edits; checked by the gating test command.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetch_paging.py","reason":"new module receiving the collect/_iter_pages/_extract_issues chain"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"drops to ~606 lines; _load_acli, _load_alert_store and _DONE_RECENT_CAP stay resident"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py","reason":"hasattr surface assertions, patch survival, truncation preserved"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","6d88-0c78-637b-4d4b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"bc3c2575-730b-431f-ae80-9c2bab3e3e9b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a33c-9001-9d86-4e59","ticket_type":"story","title":"Size relief: extract the pagination cluster from fetcher.py into fetch_paging.py","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["05dc6736-3169-4c54-ac02-fc2b47bbe809","cb6f5787-6d70-49ac-9d54-cdc5ae2f86aa","314afe83-0c4f-47d8-b44b-78544c8487ef","a891e3af-1fb5-4586-b574-3b8094d32835","962c71c7-a48b-4cb6-9ab4-a906fe2c117b","6b011396-2197-4d43-8d31-a5cd79ac9275","a5de0d64-4a1c-4415-bfaa-ef360f7ec179","bc3c2575-730b-431f-ae80-9c2bab3e3e9b","39606cc0-2952-46c9-95fc-0196d0eeaeff","493a3e75-995c-4826-909f-8efbddaa9c9c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786654754206722576,"uuid":"88c629f4-2bd2-4175-9713-65854c42b3be"}